## Background

This issue also relates to https://github.com/compio-rs/cyper/issues/25. In `compio`, a stream cannot have a `flush` request and a `shutdown` request pending at the same time. We tried to [workaround](https://github.com/compio-rs/compio/blob/a8ad4dd663f8b7cf37fc058845326a827bcc6f59/compio-io/src/compat.rs#L352) the unexpected behavior caused [here](https://github.com/hyperium/h2/blob/02eb53bb8c7416123634a0bce76e46416e9f04ad/src/codec/framed_write.rs#L168) (i.e. `poll_flush` + `poll_shutdown` in the same task `poll`), but it ended up causing more issues such as `connection`s not transitioning to `Closed` state. I guess it's better to fix the root issue in h2, hence bringing it here instead of introducing another workaround.

Regarding the fix, I would suggest adding a flag to guard [this `poll_flush` call](https://github.com/hyperium/h2/blob/02eb53bb8c7416123634a0bce76e46416e9f04ad/src/codec/framed_write.rs#L161) so that it will only be called when necessary.

